hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16701","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Israil informed us, from Simak, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr al-Qurashi, he said: one who witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he ordered the stoning of a man between Makkah and Madinah narrated to me; when the stones struck him he fled, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Why did you not leave him."
"16702","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Sanani informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to me, from his father, he said: Fannaj narrated to me, he said: I used to work in al-Daynabad and labor in it, and Yala ibn Umayya came as governor over Yemen, and with him came men from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a man from those who came with him came to me while I was in the crop diverting water in the crop, with walnuts in his sleeve; he sat on a water channel breaking and eating from those walnuts, then he beckoned to Fannaj and said: O Persian, come; so I drew near him, and the man said to Fannaj: Will you guarantee for me the planting of these walnuts by the water; Fannaj said to him: What benefit is that to me; the man said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two ears of mine say: Whoever sets up a tree and perseveres in guarding it and tending it until it bears fruit, for him in everything struck from its fruit is charity with Allah, mighty and majestic; Fannaj said: Did you yourself hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: Yes; Fannaj said: Then I guarantee it; he said: And from them are the walnuts of al-Daynabad."
